10. FPI vs FDI: Effects, Benefits and Costs
Paper: International Economics (ECNCC301) | Unit: II | Topic: FPI and FDI; effects of international capital movement; benefits and costs of FDI to home and host countries
Introduction
International capital flows take two forms: foreign portfolio investment (FPI) in shares and bonds without control, and foreign direct investment (FDI) with managerial control. Their effects on welfare and stability differ sharply.
